{% set f = falconProject %}
{% set r = falconResults %}
{% set v = f.assetVersion %}
{% set img = "/assets/imgs/falcon" %}

{# With the popup script the charts stand in the page as small tiles. This mark is set before anything is drawn. #}
<script>if ("showModal" in document.createElement("dialog")) document.documentElement.classList.add("falcon-js");</script>

<section class="falcon-hero" aria-labelledby="falcon-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects · Prototype</p>
    <p class="falcon-hero__name">FALCON <span>· Field Acoustic, Lens &amp; Climate Observation Node</span></p>
    <h1 id="falcon-title">A field node that watches, listens and measures one small place</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A box on a post beside a garden water bowl, with a camera, microphones and weather sensors. A computer
      indoors suggests a name for each animal it sees and each bird it hears, and a person checks every one.
      It is a working prototype, built at home in Kota, and the code is open source.
    </p>
    <div class="badge-row" aria-label="Project status">
      <span class="badge">Working prototype, not for sale</span>
      <span class="badge">Built 27 Oct to 10 Nov 2026</span>
      <span class="badge">Kota, Rajasthan</span>
      <span class="badge">Open source</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button-link" href="#results">Results so far</a>
      <a class="button-link button-link-secondary" href="#node">See the node</a>
      <a class="button-link button-link-light" href="#support">Support the next build</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="falcon-hero__figure">
    <img src="{{ img }}/falcon-node-hero-1000.webp?v={{ v }}" srcset="{{ img }}/falcon-node-hero-600.webp?v={{ v }} 600w, {{ img }}/falcon-node-hero-1000.webp?v={{ v }} 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 420px" width="1000" height="1250" alt="3D drawing of the FALCON node: an upright grey junction box on a post with the FALCON mark on its lid, a black camera hood low on the lid and a copper rain plate on the hood." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    <figcaption>Build 1, the node that stands in the yard. A simplified 3D drawing, not a photograph.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-label="Project status">
  <div class="falcon-status-card">
    <strong>A prototype, not a product.</strong>
    <span>
      A personal project by Vinay Chittora, who also edits MHTR.in, in a private backyard in Kota city. It is
      not inside Mukundara Hills Tiger Reserve, not a Forest Department scheme, and nothing here is for sale.
    </span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="idea" aria-labelledby="idea-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
    <h2 id="idea-title">One spot, three senses</h2>
    <p>
      Most camera traps only take pictures. FALCON also listens and measures, at one spot where animals come
      back again and again. It is not a census and it is not a security camera.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-senses">
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 12s3.5-6.5 9.5-6.5 9.5 6.5 9.5 6.5-3.5 6.5-9.5 6.5S2.5 12 2.5 12Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Lens</span>It sees what comes to the water</h3>
      <p>A camera with infrared lights watches the bowl day and night, and software suggests a name for each animal.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 10v4M8 6.5v11M12 3.5v17M16 7.5v9M20 10.5v3"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Acoustic</span>It hears what never comes into view</h3>
      <p>Microphones listen all the time and bird calls are named, so a bird that only sings is still logged.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="falcon-sense">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 13.8V5a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v8.8a4 4 0 1 1-4 0Z"/><path d="M12 9v7"/></svg>
      <h3><span>Climate</span>It notes the weather of every visit</h3>
      <p>Temperature, humidity, air pressure and rain are stored with every record.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="falcon-note falcon-note--after" id="how">
    One Ethernet cable runs out to the yard. The box captures and streams, and all the AI runs on a computer
    indoors.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Results so far</p>
    <h2 id="results-title">What the sensors told us</h2>
    <p>
      {{ r.period.from }} to {{ r.period.to }}: one yard and {{ r.period.daysWord }} days of one season, so a
      first look and not a survey. A species counts only after I have checked its recording myself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <dl class="falcon-tally falcon-tally--results" aria-label="Totals from {{ r.period.from }} to {{ r.period.to }}">
    <div><dt>Species verified</dt><dd>{{ r.totals.verified }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Seen on camera</dt><dd>{{ r.totals.onCamera }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Camera visits</dt><dd>{{ r.totalsText.cameraVisits }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Sound records</dt><dd>{{ r.totalsText.soundRecords }}</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h3 class="falcon-subhead falcon-subhead--first">Seen at the bowl</h3>
  <ul class="falcon-gallery">
    {% for p in f.frames %}
    <li>
      <figure class="falcon-thumb">
        <a href="{{ img }}/falcon-frame-{{ p.slug }}-{{ p.w }}.webp?v={{ v }}" data-falcon-pop="frames" data-w="{{ p.w }}" data-h="{{ (p.w * 0.75) | round }}">
          <span class="sr-only">Open the larger picture.</span>
          <img src="{{ img }}/falcon-frame-{{ p.slug }}-400.webp?v={{ v }}" width="400" height="300" alt="{{ p.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </a>
        <figcaption><b>{{ p.name }}</b><span>{{ p.when }}</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="falcon-note falcon-note--after">
    Frames from FALCON's own recordings, cropped and not retouched. Tap one to open it larger. The pink and
    red pictures are faults of the camera's colour, described below. The cat is the neighbourhood's domestic
    cat, which the camera's model had named a Rusty-spotted Cat.
  </p>

  <h3 class="falcon-subhead" id="species-title">All {{ r.totals.verified }} species, with counts</h3>
  {% set groups = [["Bird", "Birds"], ["Mammal", "Mammals"], ["Amphibian", "Amphibian"]] %}
  {% set countRows = (r.table | length) + (groups | length) %}
  <div class="falcon-counts-wrap" id="falcon-counts">
    <div class="falcon-counts" role="table" aria-labelledby="species-title" style="--rows-3: {{ (countRows / 3) | round(0, "ceil") }}; --rows-2: {{ (countRows / 2) | round(0, "ceil") }};">
      <div class="falcon-counts__head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">Species</span><span role="columnheader">Camera</span><span role="columnheader">Sound</span><span role="columnheader">Days</span></div>
      <div class="falcon-counts__head falcon-counts__head--2" aria-hidden="true"><span>Species</span><span>Camera</span><span>Sound</span><span>Days</span></div>
      <div class="falcon-counts__head falcon-counts__head--3" aria-hidden="true"><span>Species</span><span>Camera</span><span>Sound</span><span>Days</span></div>
      {% for g in groups %}
      <div class="falcon-counts__group" role="row"><span role="cell" aria-colspan="4">{{ g[1] }} ({{ r.totals.byGroup[g[0]] }})</span></div>
      {% for row in r.table %}{% if row.group == g[0] %}
      <div class="falcon-counts__row" role="row"><span role="rowheader"><b>{{ row.name }}</b> <i>{{ row.sci }}</i></span>{% for n in [row.camera, row.sound] %}<span role="cell">{% if n %}{{ n }}{% else %}<span aria-hidden="true">–</span><span class="sr-only">0</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}<span role="cell">{{ row.days }}</span></div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <button type="button" class="falcon-counts__more" id="falcon-counts-more" aria-controls="falcon-counts" aria-expanded="false" hidden>Show all {{ r.totals.verified }} species</button>
  {# On a phone the list starts short, with a button that opens it. Without this script it stands in full. #}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var wrap = document.getElementById("falcon-counts"), more = document.getElementById("falcon-counts-more");
      if (!wrap || !more) return;
      var label = more.textContent;
      wrap.classList.add("is-short");
      more.hidden = false;
      more.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var open = !wrap.classList.toggle("is-short");
        more.setAttribute("aria-expanded", open ? "true" : "false");
        more.textContent = open ? "Show fewer" : label;
        if (!open) document.getElementById("species-title").scrollIntoView();
      });
    })();
  </script>
  <p class="falcon-note falcon-note--after">
    Camera counts visits on camera, Sound counts sound records, and Days counts the days, out of
    {{ r.period.days }}, with a record. A dash means none.{% if r.totals.cameraUnlisted %} {{ r.text.unlisted }}{% endif %}
    {{ r.text.note }}
  </p>

  <h3 class="falcon-subhead">Highlights</h3>
  <ul class="falcon-list">
    <li><b>Most often on camera:</b> {% for s in r.regulars %}{{ s.name }} ({{ s.visits }}{% if loop.first %} visits{% endif %}){% if loop.revindex == 2 %} and {% elif not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</li>
    <li><b>Heard all day, never at the bowl:</b> Rose-ringed Parakeets, drawn by a fig tree in the yard, with {% for row in r.table %}{% if row.name == "Rose-ringed Parakeet" %}{{ row.sound }}{% endif %}{% endfor %} sound records.</li>
    <li><b>Surprises:</b> a White-breasted Waterhen, a bird of wet ground, on {{ r.notable.waterhen.date }} at {{ r.notable.waterhen.time }}, and a Rhesus Macaque on {{ r.notable.macaque.date }} at {{ r.notable.macaque.time }}, the first monkey on FALCON's record.</li>
    <li><b>Shy, and a regular:</b> the Bluethroat, a winter visitor, came {{ r.notable.bluethroat.visits }} times on {{ r.notable.bluethroat.cameraDays }} of the {{ r.notable.bluethroat.daysSinceFirst }} days since {{ r.notable.bluethroat.date }}, most of them between 15:00 and 17:00.</li>
    <li><b>Back again:</b> a Sulphur-bellied Warbler on {{ r.notable.warbler.date }}. I photographed one in this yard last year too.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="falcon-subhead">When the bowl is busy</h3>
  {% set heats = [
    { key: "camera", title: "Camera visits", unit: "visits", one: "visit" },
    { key: "sound", title: "Sound records", unit: "records", one: "record" }
  ] %}
  <div class="falcon-two falcon-busy">
    <ul class="falcon-list">
      <li><b>Camera:</b> busiest from 08:00 to 10:00 and again from 14:00 to 17:00.</li>
      <li><b>Sound:</b> the calls start at dawn. Most come between 06:00 and 10:00 and in the hour from 17:00, and the parakeets are the loudest at both ends of the day.</li>
      <li><b>Weather:</b> {{ r.weatherRange.min }} to {{ r.weatherRange.max }} °C, and a wet rain plate on {{ r.weatherRange.wetDaysWord }} days only. The bowl is quietest in the warmest hours, but those are also the middle of the day, so no weather pattern can be claimed yet.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="falcon-heat-tiles">
      <ul class="falcon-gallery falcon-gallery--problems">
        {% for h in heats %}
        <li>
          <button type="button" class="falcon-heat-tile falcon-heat--{{ h.key }}" data-falcon-pop="charts" data-pop-target="falcon-heat-{{ h.key }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 {{ r[h.key] | length }}" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <g transform="translate(.07 .07)">{% for row in r[h.key] %}{% set y = loop.index0 %}{% for c in row.cells %}{% if c.l %}<rect class="l{{ c.l }}" x="{{ loop.index0 }}" y="{{ y }}" width=".86" height=".86"/>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</g>
            </svg>
            <span class="falcon-heat-tile__text"><b>{{ h.title }}</b><span>by day and hour</span></span>
            <span class="sr-only">Open this chart large, with its numbers.</span>
          </button>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
        <li>
          <button type="button" class="falcon-heat-tile falcon-heat--species" data-falcon-pop="charts" data-pop-target="falcon-heat-species">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 {{ r.species | length }}" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <g transform="translate(.07 .07)">{% for row in r.species %}{% set y = loop.index0 %}{% for c in row.cells %}{% if c.l %}<rect class="l{{ c.l }}" x="{{ loop.index0 }}" y="{{ y }}" width=".86" height=".86"/>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</g>
            </svg>
            <span class="falcon-heat-tile__text"><b>Top eight species</b><span>hour by hour</span></span>
            <span class="sr-only">Open this chart large, with its numbers.</span>
          </button>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="falcon-note">Tap a chart to open it large, with its numbers.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {# The charts at full size. The popup shows a copy of each. Without the popup script they stand here in the page. #}
  <div class="falcon-heat-store">
    <div class="falcon-two falcon-heats">
      {% for h in heats %}
      <figure class="falcon-heat falcon-heat--{{ h.key }}" id="falcon-heat-{{ h.key }}">
        <figcaption>{{ h.title }}, by day and hour <span>Each square is one hour of one day.</span></figcaption>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Day</span></th>{% for hr in r.hours %}<th scope="col">{% if hr % 6 == 0 %}{{ hr }}{% else %}<span class="sr-only">{{ hr }}</span>{% endif %}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for row in r[h.key] %}
              <tr><th scope="row">{{ row.label }}</th>{% for c in row.cells %}<td class="l{{ c.l }}" title="{{ row.label }}, {% if loop.index0 < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ loop.index0 }}:00, {{ c.n }} {% if c.n == 1 %}{{ h.one }}{% else %}{{ h.unit }}{% endif %}"><span class="falcon-heat__n">{{ c.n }}</span></td>{% endfor %}</tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="falcon-heat-key" aria-hidden="true">
          <span><i class="l0"></i>none</span><span><i class="l1"></i>1–2</span><span><i class="l2"></i>3–5</span><span><i class="l3"></i>6–11</span><span><i class="l4"></i>12 or more</span>
        </p>
      </figure>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figure class="falcon-heat falcon-heat--species" id="falcon-heat-species">
      <figcaption>The eight commonest species, hour by hour <span>Seen and heard. Each row is shaded against that species' own busiest hour.</span></figcaption>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Species</span></th>{% for hr in r.hours %}<th scope="col">{% if hr % 3 == 0 %}{{ hr }}{% else %}<span class="sr-only">{{ hr }}</span>{% endif %}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in r.species %}
            <tr><th scope="row">{{ row.label }} <small>{{ row.total }}, {{ row.how }}</small></th>{% for c in row.cells %}<td class="l{{ c.l }}" title="{{ row.label }}, {% if loop.index0 < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ loop.index0 }}:00, {{ c.n }} {% if c.n == 1 %}record{% else %}records{% endif %}"><span class="falcon-heat__n">{{ c.n }}</span></td>{% endfor %}</tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="falcon-heat-key" aria-hidden="true">
        <span><i class="l0"></i>none</span><span><i class="l1"></i><i class="l2"></i><i class="l3"></i><i class="l4"></i>from few to that species' busiest hour</span>
      </p>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h3 class="falcon-subhead">What FALCON does by itself, and what I do</h3>
  <div class="falcon-two falcon-fix">
    <ul class="falcon-list">
      <li><b>Capturing is automatic.</b> FALCON recorded every one of the {{ r.rates.camera.realText }} verified camera visits and {{ r.rates.sound.realText }} verified sound records by itself, each with its recording and the weather at that moment.</li>
      <li><b>By sound, the names hold.</b> When BirdNET heard a real bird, its name was right for {{ r.rates.sound.rightText }} of the {{ r.rates.sound.realText }} records ({{ r.rates.sound.percent }} %). Street and household noise is still sometimes named as a bird, so every record gets a check.</li>
      <li><b>From the picture, the names are the weak point.</b> With this webcam the suggested name was often wrong, and I named most visits myself from the recordings. The picture is poor in low light, pink on many mornings and off in colour: a Bluethroat's throat did not look blue. I put this down to the camera, not to the AI models.</li>
      <li><b>What is being done.</b> This is why the first support money went into a better camera and microphone for Build 2.</li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="falcon-gallery falcon-gallery--problems">
      {% for p in f.problemFrames %}
      <li>
        <figure class="falcon-thumb">
          <a href="{{ img }}/falcon-frame-{{ p.slug }}-{{ p.w }}.webp?v={{ v }}" data-falcon-pop="faults" data-w="{{ p.w }}" data-h="{{ (p.w * 0.75) | round }}">
            <span class="sr-only">Open the larger picture.</span>
            <img src="{{ img }}/falcon-frame-{{ p.slug }}-400.webp?v={{ v }}" width="400" height="300" alt="{{ p.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>
          <figcaption><b>{{ p.title }}</b><span>{{ p.text }}</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="falcon-two falcon-two--even">
    <div>
      <h3 class="falcon-subhead">Two weeks of tuning</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li><b>Where it started.</b> On the first night 133 “visits” were house geckos under wrong names. The camera's model chose from 14,367 species of all India.</li>
        <li><b>Calibrated.</b> The camera now chooses from 1,384 species recorded in Rajasthan, and BirdNET names only birds recorded there. The picture controls were tuned and the microphone was measured.</li>
        <li><b>Improved.</b> Each stay at the water is one recording with its sound. A sound is announced only when a cleaned copy of it agrees on the bird. Damaged frames are thrown away.</li>
        <li><b>Rats spoiled five nights.</b> I put grain near the bowl, and from 19 November rats raided it every night: at least {% for n in r.rats %}{{ n.visits }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} visits. Their records were deleted, rats at night are no longer logged, and there will be no more feed near the bowl.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="falcon-subhead">Known limits</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li>Night vision reaches about a metre, and insects in it cannot be named.</li>
        <li>A name counts only after a person has checked it, and reviewing is the slowest part.</li>
        <li>It needs a PC with an NVIDIA graphics card indoors.</li>
        <li>The box is drilled by hand and has not been through a monsoon or a summer.</li>
        <li>It logs visits to one spot. It does not count animals or estimate populations.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if r.reportUrl %}
  <p class="falcon-note falcon-note--after">
    The full species table, with scientific names, methods and limits, is in the
    <a href="{{ r.reportUrl }}">field report</a>.
  </p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="section" id="node" aria-labelledby="node-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The node, part by part</p>
    <h2 id="node-title">A junction box, a hood and one cable</h2>
    <p>
      Five views of Build 1 with its parts numbered. It is a simplified drawing made from photographs of the
      real node, not a CAD file, and positions inside the box are approximate.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="falcon-viewer" data-falcon-viewer data-tabs-label="Views of the node" data-3d-label="Turn it round in 3D" data-three="/assets/js/falcon/three-r128.min.js?v={{ v }}" data-model="/assets/js/falcon/falcon-node-model.js?v={{ v }}">
    {% for view in f.views %}
    {% set lay = falconNodeLayout.views[view.id] %}
    <figure class="falcon-view" id="node-{{ view.id }}" data-view="{{ view.id }}" data-tab="{{ view.tab }}">
      <div class="falcon-stage">
        <picture>
          <source media="(max-width: 620px)" srcset="{{ img }}/node-{{ view.id }}-tall-720.webp?v={{ v }} 720w, {{ img }}/node-{{ view.id }}-tall-1200.webp?v={{ v }} 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="1500">
          <img src="{{ img }}/node-{{ view.id }}-wide-1400.webp?v={{ v }}" srcset="{{ img }}/node-{{ view.id }}-wide-800.webp?v={{ v }} 800w, {{ img }}/node-{{ view.id }}-wide-1400.webp?v={{ v }} 1400w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 640px" width="1400" height="1050" alt="{{ view.alt }}"{% if not loop.first %} loading="lazy"{% endif %} decoding="async">
        </picture>
        {% if lay %}
        {% for key in ["wide", "tall"] %}
        <svg class="falcon-leaders falcon-leaders--{{ key }}" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          {% for c in view.callouts %}{% set p = lay[key][c.id] %}<line data-callout="{{ c.id }}" x1="{{ p.ax }}" y1="{{ p.ay }}" x2="{{ p.lx }}" y2="{{ p.ly }}"/>{% endfor %}
        </svg>
        {% endfor %}
        <ol class="falcon-markers" aria-hidden="true">
          {% for c in view.callouts %}{% set w = lay.wide[c.id] %}{% set t = lay.tall[c.id] %}
          <li data-callout="{{ c.id }}" style="--wx:{{ w.lx }}%;--wy:{{ w.ly }}%;--wax:{{ w.ax }}%;--way:{{ w.ay }}%;--tx:{{ t.lx }}%;--ty:{{ t.ly }}%;--tax:{{ t.ax }}%;--tay:{{ t.ay }}%"><span class="falcon-dot"></span><span class="falcon-num">{{ loop.index }}</span></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <h3>{{ view.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ view.intro }}</p>
        <ol class="falcon-legend">
          {% for c in view.callouts %}
          <li data-callout="{{ c.id }}"><b>{{ c.name }}.</b> {{ c.text }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="hardware" aria-labelledby="hardware-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Parts and AI models</p>
    <h2 id="hardware-title">Off-the-shelf parts and open models</h2>
    <p>
      Every part of Build 1 can be bought. The box was drilled by hand, and that shell is the part to
      replace first.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-two falcon-two--even">
    <div>
      <h3>Parts of Build 1</h3>
      <dl class="falcon-licences falcon-parts">
        {% for row in f.hardware %}
        <div><dt>{{ row.part }}</dt><dd>{{ row.short }}</dd></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>AI models</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li><b>MegaDetector V6</b> finds animals, people and vehicles in the picture.</li>
        <li><b>BioCLIP 2.5</b> suggests the species, from the 1,384 recorded in Rajasthan on iNaturalist.</li>
        <li><b>BirdNET V2.4</b> names bird calls, and only birds recorded in Rajasthan. Any other call is kept as an unidentified sound for me to check.</li>
        <li>All three run on the computer at home. Nothing is sent to a cloud service, and my corrections do not retrain the models.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="interface" aria-labelledby="interface-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The interface</p>
    <h2 id="interface-title">Live for watching, Review for checking</h2>
    <p>
      Screenshots of the real dashboard, taken on 24 November 2026. Tap or click one to open it at full size.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-shots falcon-shots--grid">
    {% for shot in f.shots %}
    <figure class="falcon-shot">
      <a class="falcon-shot__image" href="{{ img }}/falcon-{{ shot.id }}-{{ shot.w }}.webp?v={{ v }}" data-falcon-pop="screens" data-w="{{ shot.w }}" data-h="{{ shot.h }}">
        <span class="sr-only">Open the full-size screenshot.</span>
        <img src="{{ img }}/falcon-{{ shot.id }}-800.webp?v={{ v }}" width="800" height="{{ shot.smallH }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        <h3>{{ shot.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ shot.text }}</p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="rules" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it decides and what it shares</p>
    <h2 id="rules-title">A name has to be earned</h2>
    <p>
      A few records you can trust are worth more than many doubtful ones.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-two falcon-two--even">
    <div>
      <h3>How it decides</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li><b>Likely.</b> Several frames over about two seconds agree on one species. Only these appear on the Live page.</li>
        <li><b>Probable or possible.</b> Look-alikes and faint guesses wait on the Review page and are never announced.</li>
        <li><b>Confirmed.</b> Only a person can confirm a record, after watching or listening to it.</li>
        <li>The number beside a name is a similarity score, not a probability.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 id="inaturalist">What it shares</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li>A visit that I have checked can be posted to <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">iNaturalist</a>, where other people can check the name. The first two were <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/415043198" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">an Oriental Magpie-Robin</a> and <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/415042739" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">a Bluethroat</a>.</li>
        <li>Nothing is posted automatically. Every post takes my press of the Post button.</li>
        <li>The location is obscured: the public sees a random point inside a box about 20 km across, never the yard.</li>
        <li>Checked records can also be exported as <a href="https://camtrap-dp.tdwg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Camtrap DP</a>, the open format for camera-trap data.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Where it is going</p>
    <h2 id="roadmap-title">From a backyard rig to something others can host</h2>
    <p>
      The aim is a device that a friend, a school or a field researcher can plug in and use without a
      desktop PC or any technical setup.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-plan">
    {% for state in ["Done", "In progress", "Needs support", "Later"] %}
    {% set stateClass = "falcon-state--" + (state | lower | replace(" ", "-")) %}
    <div class="falcon-plan__group {{ stateClass }}">
      <h3 class="falcon-state {{ stateClass }}">{{ state }}</h3>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        {% for step in f.roadmap %}{% if step.state == state %}
        <li>{% if step.short %}<b>{{ step.name }}.</b> {{ step.short }}{% else %}{{ step.name }}{% endif %}</li>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section falcon-support" id="support" aria-labelledby="support-title">
  <div class="falcon-support__panel">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support the next build</p>
      <h2 id="support-title">Two pieces of equipment would move this forward</h2>
      <p>
        Build 1 leans on a desktop PC and a shell made by hand. Two purchases would turn it into something
        other people can copy. Prices are from Indian sellers on {{ f.pricesChecked }}.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="falcon-asks">
      <article class="falcon-ask">
        <h3>A small computer for the AI</h3>
        <p class="falcon-ask__price">about ₹65,000 to ₹70,000</p>
        <ul class="falcon-list">
          <li>An NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super kit with a drive, a fan case and a Wi-Fi card, so that a home, a school or a field station without a gaming PC can host a node.</li>
          <li>FALCON has not run on a Jetson yet. It has to give the same answers as the PC on nights already recorded, and the result goes on this page either way.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="falcon-ask">
        <h3>A simple 3D printer</h3>
        <p class="falcon-ask__price">about ₹25,000 to ₹30,000</p>
        <ul class="falcon-list">
          <li>A small desktop printer such as the Bambu Lab A1 mini, for a camera hood, sensor holders and a post mount that other people can print and copy.</li>
          <li>The first prints are tried on the node in the yard. Which plastic stands a Kota summer is part of the test.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="falcon-total">
      <p><strong>{{ f.fund.goal }}</strong>for both, with the smaller parts they need.</p>
      <a class="button-link" href="{{ f.supportUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contribute on Buy Me a Coffee</a>
    </div>

    <dl class="falcon-tally" aria-label="Running total">
      <div><dt>Received for FALCON</dt><dd>{{ f.fund.received }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Spent</dt><dd>{{ f.fund.spent }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Bought so far</dt><dd>{{ f.fund.bought }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Updated</dt><dd>{{ f.fund.updated }}</dd></div>
    </dl>

    {% if f.fund.supporters and f.fund.supporters.length %}
    <div class="falcon-thanks">
      <h3 id="thanks-title">Thank you</h3>
      <p class="falcon-note">The people who have supported FALCON so far.</p>
      <ul class="falcon-mugs" aria-labelledby="thanks-title">
        {# A first name of twelve letters or more is fitted to the width of the mug. #}
        {% for s in f.fund.supporters %}{% set n = s.first | length %}
        <li class="falcon-mug">
          <span class="falcon-mug__name">{{ s.name }}</span>
          <svg class="falcon-mug__cup" viewBox="0 0 158 96" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path class="falcon-mug__steam" fill="none" d="M45 20c-6-5 6-9 0-15M68 20c-6-5 6-9 0-15M91 20c-6-5 6-9 0-15"/>
            <path class="falcon-mug__handle" fill="none" d="M124 42h7a13 13 0 0 1 0 26h-7"/>
            <path class="falcon-mug__body" d="M12 28h112v42a16 16 0 0 1-16 16H28a16 16 0 0 1-16-16z"/>
            <text class="falcon-mug__first{% if n > 14 %} falcon-mug__first--small{% endif %}" x="68" y="57" dy="0.35em" text-anchor="middle"{% if n > 11 %} textLength="98" lengthAdjust="spacingAndGlyphs"{% endif %}>{{ s.first }}</text>
          </svg>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="falcon-terms">
      <div>
        <h3>How the money is handled</h3>
        <ul class="falcon-list">
          <li>Contributions go through the Cane &amp; Camera page on Buy Me a Coffee, which also supports the upkeep of MHTR.in. <b>Please write FALCON in your message</b>. Without that word the money goes to the upkeep of the site.</li>
          <li><b>A change of plan.</b> The first money went into Build 2's camera and microphone instead of the printer, because the results above showed that the webcam and the old microphone held FALCON back most. From here on, money marked FALCON goes to the two items above, the printer first.</li>
          <li>The running total is updated by hand whenever money comes in or something is bought. If less comes in than the computer costs, that money stays set aside for it, and this page will say how much is there.</li>
          <li>This is a personal project, not a registered charity. A contribution is a gift: no rewards, no shares, no device in return and no tax benefit.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Other ways to help</h3>
        <ul class="falcon-list">
          <li><b>Lend hardware:</b> a Jetson you no longer use, or a few hours on your own 3D printer.</li>
          <li><b>Lend your ears:</b> check a few short recordings of night calls around Kota.</li>
          <li><b>Try the code</b> on your own computer and report where it breaks.</li>
          <li><b>Check the names</b> of FALCON's posts on iNaturalist, such as the <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/415042739" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluethroat of 16 November</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="falcon-note">Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="code" aria-labelledby="code-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
    <h2 id="code-title">Build one, or help build the next</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="falcon-two">
    <div>
      <ul class="falcon-list">
        <li>Everything written for FALCON is in one public repository: the node service, the application that runs the models, the dashboard and about 700 automated tests.</li>
        <li>Build 1 is tagged v1.0. The work done since then follows as the next release when its testing at home is finished.</li>
        <li>Free software under the GNU AGPL, version 3. If you pass on a changed version, or run one for other people, you share your changes under the same licence, keep the author credit and give your version its own name.</li>
        <li>The models are downloaded, and each keeps its own licence. The BirdNET model is for non-commercial use only, so anyone thinking of selling a device has to replace it or license it.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button-link" href="{{ f.repoUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FALCON on GitHub</a>
        <a class="button-link button-link-secondary" href="{{ f.repoUrl }}/tree/v1.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Build 1 (v1.0)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="falcon-licences" aria-label="Licences">
      <div><dt>FALCON code</dt><dd>GNU AGPL version 3, with <a href="{{ f.repoUrl }}/blob/main/ADDITIONAL-TERMS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">terms on author credit and naming</a>. Build 1 (v1.0): Apache 2.0.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>MegaDetector V6</dt><dd>MIT variant, through PyTorchWildlife.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>BioCLIP 2.5</dt><dd>MIT.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>BirdNET V2.4</dt><dd>Code MIT; model CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which means non-commercial use only.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="care" aria-labelledby="care-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Care and privacy</p>
    <h2 id="care-title">It watches wildlife, not people</h2>
  </div>
  <ul class="falcon-list">
    <li>People are never saved as observations. By default a person in the picture is covered with a grey box, and human voices are silenced in saved sound. These filters can miss, so anyone who hosts a node should still tell the people who live there and the neighbours within earshot.</li>
    <li>The models run on the owner's computer. A record leaves it only when the owner exports it or posts it to iNaturalist.</li>
    <li>This node stands in a private backyard in Kota city. Inside a protected area a device like it needs written permission from the Forest Department.</li>
    <li>This page gives the place only as Kota, Rajasthan, and the posts on iNaturalist carry an obscured location.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

